{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 10, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e2b-it", "content": "Arthur awoke to the familiar chirping of birds, but something felt…off. The sunlight streaming through his window was too perfect, the colors of the morning light unnaturally vibrant. He stretched, and his limbs felt strangely… responsive. A quick glance at his reflection in the mirror revealed a subtle difference – his eyes were a shade brighter, almost glowing. He tried to recall the events of the previous day, a mundane routine of spreadsheets and lukewarm coffee, but his mind felt strangely blank, like a freshly wiped slate. Then he noticed it: a small, almost imperceptible shimmer in the air near his desk, and a faint, pixelated outline of a keyboard hovering just beyond his reach. Panic began to claw at his throat as he realized the impossible: he wasn't in his apartment anymore. He was *in* a video game.\n\n***\n\nHe stumbled out of bed, the floor feeling strangely solid and textured beneath his feet. The world outside his window wasn't the familiar cityscape; it was a lush, vibrant forest, rendered in hyper-realistic detail. A small, wooden signpost appeared before him, displaying the words \"Welcome to Eldoria – Player Name: Arthur.\" He felt a surge of bewildered frustration, followed by a strange sense of detachment. This wasn't a dream; it was real. He was Arthur, a character in someone else’s meticulously crafted world. He had no skills, no history, no purpose beyond the parameters of this digital reality. A small, winged creature, resembling a digital hummingbird, zipped past his face, leaving a trail of sparkling dust. He took a shaky breath, the air thick with the scent of pine and something… manufactured. His adventure had begun, and he had no idea where it would lead.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Arthur", "logprob": -0.6147120594978333}, {"token": "▁awoke", "logprob": -0.5340976119041443}, {"token": "▁to", "logprob": -0.002990062581